DON'T.  Robert E. Howard was a great writer, and I really enjoyed the
world he created.  A consistent world, described with more detail than
it was the case for Tolkien (on the other hand, Tolkien put more stress
on languages).
However, in the popular opinion, Howard's books are a pile of mindless
hack&slash prose.  It's an untrue view, caused by 4897984364398 or so
random authors who copied the name of Conan and basically nothing more.
The movies just belong to this pile.

To cloud things even more, after Howard's death his literary agent took
most of Howard's unfinished and/or published but set with different
characters, in a different world and simply changed the names to make
the works have "Conan" in them.  It's nothing but a cheap cash run,
trying to exploit the franchise.

Read the books, instead, paying heed to any footnotes.  If Sprague De
Camp or Lin Carter are mentioned, the book in question was tampered with.
The original stuff is certainly worth reading.

